# Beads passive exports — union-merge to eliminate spurious git conflicts.
#
# Dolt (synced via refs/dolt/data) is the source of truth; these JSONL files are
# regenerated snapshots that bd re-exports on most git operations. Two divergent
# regenerations of the same logical state otherwise collide under git's default
# line merge (see the rate-sheet-merge incident, 2026-05-30).
#
# `merge=union` keeps both sides' lines with no conflict markers — the automation
# of the beads FAQ's official "keep both lines" resolution. It is safe here because
# each line is one complete JSON record (JSONL), hash-based issue IDs (archie-xxxx)
# never collide across branches, and Dolt dedupes by ID so any transient duplicate
# line self-heals on the next `bd dolt pull` / export. Do NOT hand-reconcile these
# files; the authoritative data lives in Dolt, never in the export text.
#
# Refs: beads FAQ "How do I handle merge conflicts?"; docs/SYNC_CONCEPTS.md.
issues.jsonl        merge=union
interactions.jsonl  merge=union
events.jsonl        merge=union
